            "summary": "On '{{v1}}' I opened Dashboard settings → {{v3}} and set Auto {{v4}} to \"1m\", saved (\"Dashboard saved\"), then selected 1m in the top-bar {{v4}} picker and saved again with \"Update default {{v4}} value\" ticked so it persists. The required verification — the settings page after reload — confirms it: after a full page reload the settings page shows Auto {{v4}} = \"1m\" (input#auto-refresh-input), and the top-bar {{v4}} menu offers exactly Off / Auto / 1m with 1m in effect (URL carries {{v4}}=1m). Title, tag \"bench\" and time range (Last 6 hours / now-6h) are unchanged. Additionally noted: the JSON Model Monaco pane in this Grafana build only renders one visible line at a time, so the settings-after-reload route (explicitly allowed by the instruction) was used for verification; a failed find-box step had typed the text \"{{v4}}\" into the JSON Model editor, and that local edit was never saved — the reload discarded it and all post-reload reads show the persisted model intact. URL: http://127.0.0.1:3000/d/{{v5}}/{{v6}}. (auto_refresh_in_settings_after_reload: Settings → {{v3}} → Auto {{v4}}, input#auto-refresh-input)",
